  "pattern": "off-by-one",
  "difficulty_rating": 2125,
  "explanation": "The right half is taken from mid + 1 instead of mid, so the element sitting at the midpoint is dropped at every split level. The recursion still terminates, but rebuilding [1,2,3,4,5] keeps only [1,4] — the midpoints 2, 3 and 5 are silently lost.",
  "prompt": "This recursively splits a list in half and re-joins the halves. Step through the recursion and predict what the rebuilt list contains.",
  "language": "javascript",
  "snippet": "function splitHalves(items) {\n  if (items.length <= 1) {\n    return items.slice(0, 1);\n  }\n  const mid = Math.floor(items.length / 2);\n  const left = splitHalves(items.slice(0, mid));\n  const right = splitHalves(items.slice(mid + 1));\n  return left.concat(right);\n}\nconst rebuilt = splitHalves([1, 2, 3, 4, 5]);\nconsole.log(\"rebuilt:\", rebuilt.join(\",\"));\nconsole.log(\"count:\", rebuilt.length);",
